% ======================================================================================== 4 Methodology
\section{Methodology}\label{sec:method}
\para{Fast tier and v2} A detector fires on a \(\geq\)<< V('pol.det_c') >>¢ move of the 10\,s VWAP against the prior
60\,s. Each month a wallet qualifies on past months only (\(\geq\)<< V('pol.q_prints') >> prints 0--3\,s after a
detection, \(\geq\)<< V('pol.q_matches') >> matches, \(t > << V('pol.q_t') >>\)). The frozen book v2 copies their
prints, sized by resolution risk, at most << V('risk.order_usd') >> an order and << V('risk.netcap') >> shares net per
match, held to resolution, at the fast tier's own prices: \emph{the opportunity at their speed, not our execution}
(components: Table~\ref{tab:comp}).

\para{CV and the latency budget} Frame to unsigned order takes << V('e2e.ours') >>\,ms; with a simulated 1\,s feed,
<< V('e2e.net') >>\,ms network and the 1\,s venue hold an order is executable at << V('e2e.total') >>\,ms, inside the
organiser's 3\,s bar (Fig.~\ref{fig:f2t}; paper, no order sent). It wins only if
\begin{equation}\label{eq:budget}
  V + \delta + D - \ell \;<\; L + R \quad\Longleftrightarrow\quad V \;<\; L + R - D - \delta + \ell ,
\end{equation}
where \(V\) is the feed delay, \(\delta\) our pipeline and network, \(D\) the << V('venue.delay') >>\,s taker delay,
\(\ell\) the call lead, \(L\) the stamp lag and \(R\) the reprice relative to the stamp (measured, \(n =
<< V('lat.n_points') >>\)). The trade set is the historical \(\geq\)<< V('pol.det_c') >>¢ detector set,
\emph{selected on outcomes, not ex ante}; the replay calls every point. \(L\) is unmeasured; Table~\ref{tab:head} shows
every reading. Only \(L + R\) enters, so \(V = 1\)\,s at the post hoc \(L = << V('cv.cal.lag') >>\)\,s equals a camera
<< V('cv.cal.shift') >>\,s ahead of the point at \(L = << V('cv.pre.lag') >>\)\,s.

\para{Costs} Each match's own taker fee, \(f(q) = r\,q\,(1-q)\) per share \(= 10{,}000\,r\,(1-q)\) bps of notional,
\(r = << V('fee.rate') >>\) today; spreads are paid as traded; Table~\ref{tab:fail} doubles them. \para{Validation} Walk-forward inside IS; the fee in force; every read of held-out data logged.

