\para{Sharpe above 3} We assumed a bug and found one: fixing the onset look-ahead (D9) cut IS Sharpe from
<< V('v2.onset.is.sr') >> to << V('v2.is.sr') >>. The rest is about << V('v2.trades_per_day') >> small, nearly
independent bets a day. The deflated Sharpe \citep{bailey2014} is << V('v2.is.dsr') >> IS but << V('v2.oos.dsr') >>
OOS: 40 days cannot rule out luck.
\para{Latency scenarios} Pre-registered, the CV trader makes << V('sc.pre.oos.v05.usd') >>, << V('sc.pre.oos.v1.usd') >>
and << V('sc.pre.oos.v3.usd') >> a day held out at 0.5, 1 and 3\,s (Table~\ref{tab:head}B, Fig.~\ref{fig:speed}); post
