\section{Risk management}\label{sec:risk}
\begin{itemize}
\item \textbf{Limits, in code; de-risking, set in advance.} << V('risk.order_usd') >> per order,
<< V('risk.netcap') >> shares net per match, zone << V('risk.zone') >>: one match can lose at most
<< V('risk.maxloss') >> plus fees. Kill switches: stale feed \(>\)<< V('risk.feed_stale') >>\,s, vision
\(>\)<< V('risk.vision_stale') >>\,s, latency above its rolling p95; a << V('risk.daily_stop') >> daily stop. Halve
size if the trailing 30-day edge is below << V('pol.trail_half') >>¢; stop at \(\leq 0\), a << V('pol.dd_stop') >>
drawdown, or a fee or delay change.
\item \textbf{CV model risk.} Wrong calls always fill; MISS calls trade only at confidence \(\geq\)0.95, and a
confirmed false call halts the day. Phantom calls outside play (about << V('cv.phantom.hr') >> an hour) would erase the
1\,s OOS P\&L at << V('cv.phantom.pre') >> (pre-registered) or << V('cv.phantom.cal') >> (post hoc) a day; a
rally-state gate is coded but not yet evaluated.
\item \textbf{Tail, venue, legal.} The UMA oracle settles
\citep{pmuma}; US persons are close-only \citep{pmgeoblock}; courtsiding breaches ticket terms \citep{itf2026}.
Factors \citep{fama1993,carhart1997}: \(\alpha\) \(t = << V('fac.alpha_t') >>\), max \(|t| = << V('fac.max_t') >>\).
\end{itemize}

