\section{Liquidity and capacity}\label{sec:liq}
v2 trades << V('v2.is.notional_day') >> a day, << V('v2.is.share_vol') >> of match volume; its OOS CI excludes zero
only up to 1\(\times\) size (<< V('cap.1x.oos.capital') >>) and 5\(\times\) loses. The CV book at the pre-registered lag
has Sharpe << V('capcv.pre.sr0.is') >>\,/\,<< V('capcv.pre.sr0.oos') >> (IS\,/\,OOS) at its smallest size: no capacity.
Post hoc, its Sharpe halves at << V('capcv.half.oos') >> of capital OOS and << V('capcv.half.is') >> IS
(Fig.~\ref{fig:capacity}); \$/day peaks at << V('capcv.pmax.oos.day') >> on << V('capcv.pmax.oos') >> OOS (Sharpe
<< V('capcv.pmax.oos.sr') >>). It trades << V('capcv.share_inplay') >> of in-play volume but << V('capcv.share_fast') >>
of the fast tier's 0--3\,s volume: the seconds after each point bind. The cheapest data
stack (<< V('fin.fixed.low') >> a day) needs << V('capcv.low.oos') >>--<< V('capcv.low.is') >> of capital post hoc; at
1\,s the book can pay at most << V('cv.cal.oos.maxlic') >> a month for data post hoc and << V('cv.pre.oos.maxlic') >>
pre-registered, against quotes of << V('fin.feed.low') >>--<< V('fin.feed.high') >>. At today's fee COURTSIDE prices
speed; it is not yet a business.

% ======================================================================================== 8 Limitations
\section{Limitations and next steps}\label{sec:limits}
One number, the stamp lag \(L\), moves the break-even one for one (Eq.~\ref{eq:budget}); its post hoc value assumes
human reaction, but the 1\,s hold dominates (\(L \geq << V('cv.L_bot') >>\)\,s even for a 20\,ms bot). One session with
a licensed feed and test orders measures \(L\) and whether delayed orders are released on a 1\,s clock. Licensing that
feed is a purchase decision, not yet a deployment: sub-second video is sold to licensed sportsbooks, and at 1\,s the
book covers the cheapest data quote only if \(L \geq << V('cv.L_go') >>\)\,s. CV accuracy is from table tennis; tennis
is simulated; no order was ever sent.\label{lastmain}

