\section*{Calculations}\label{sec:calc}
Every statistic in the paper, its formula and one worked example with our numbers (source keys in
\texttt{results/paper/numbers.json}).

\para{C1. Annualised Sharpe} \(\text{SR} = \sqrt{365}\,\bar d / s_d\), where \(d_t\) is the daily net P\&L on every
calendar day of the period (zero on days without trades) and \(s_d\) its standard deviation (\(n-1\)). v2 IS:
\(\bar d = << V('calc.is.mean') >>\), \(s_d = << V('calc.is.sd') >>\), \(T = << V('calc.is.T') >>\) days, so
\(\text{SR}_\text{d} = << V('calc.is.srd') >>\) and \(\text{SR} = << V('calc.is.srd') >> \times << V('calc.sqrt365') >> =
<< V('calc.is.sr') >>\). OOS: \(<< V('calc.oos.mean') >> / << V('calc.oos.sd') >> \times << V('calc.sqrt365') >> =
<< V('calc.oos.sr') >>\).

\para{C2. Sortino} \(\sqrt{365}\,\bar d / \text{DD}\), \(\text{DD} = \sqrt{\tfrac1T\sum_t \min(d_t,0)^2}\). v2 OOS:
\(\text{DD} = << V('calc.so.dd') >>\), so \(\sqrt{365}\times << V('calc.oos.mean') >> / << V('calc.so.dd') >> =
<< V('calc.so') >>\).

\para{C3. Maximum drawdown} \(\text{MDD} = \min_t \big(E_t - \max_{s\le t} E_s\big)\), \(E_t = \sum_{u\le t} d_u\),
reported as a share of capital. v2 OOS: \(<< V('calc.mdd') >> / << V('calc.oos.cap') >> = << V('calc.mdd.pct') >>\).

\para{C4. Probabilistic Sharpe} \(\text{PSR}(\text{SR}^*) = \Phi\!\Big((\widehat{\text{SR}}-\text{SR}^*)\sqrt{T-1}\,\big/\sqrt{1-\gamma_3\widehat{\text{SR}}+\tfrac{\gamma_4-1}{4}\widehat{\text{SR}}^2}\Big)\)
on daily SR, skew \(\gamma_3\) and kurtosis \(\gamma_4\) \citep{bailey2014}. v2 OOS: \(\widehat{\text{SR}} =
<< V('calc.oos.srd') >>\), \(T = << V('calc.oos.T') >>\), \(\gamma_3 = << V('calc.oos.skew') >>\), \(\gamma_4 =
<< V('calc.oos.kurt') >>\): \(\text{PSR}(0) = << V('calc.psr0') >>\).

\para{C5. Deflated Sharpe} \(\text{DSR} = \text{PSR}(\text{SR}_0)\) with \(\text{SR}_0 = \sqrt{V}\big((1-\gamma)\Phi^{-1}(1-\tfrac1N) + \gamma\,\Phi^{-1}(1-\tfrac{1}{Ne})\big)\),
\(\gamma\) the Euler--Mascheroni constant and \(N\) the trial count. v2 OOS, \(N = << V('rig.N3386') >>\), null
variance \(V = 1/(T-1)\): \(\Phi^{-1}\) terms << V('calc.z1') >> and << V('calc.z2') >>, \(\text{SR}_0 = << V('calc.sr0d') >>\)
daily (<< V('calc.sr0a') >> annualised), DSR \(= << V('calc.dsr') >>\). Table~\ref{tab:head} reports the lowest DSR
over three variance sources.

\para{C6. Probability of backtest overfitting} CSCV \citep{bailey2017}: split the daily P\&L of \(<< V('rig.pbo.n') >>\)
variants into \(S = << V('rig.pbo.S') >>\) blocks; for each of the \(\binom{16}{8} = << V('rig.pbo.splits') >>\)
halvings pick the IS-best variant and take the logit \(\lambda = \ln\frac{\omega}{1-\omega}\) of its OOS rank
\(\omega\); PBO \(= \Pr(\lambda \le 0)\). v2-safe grid: PBO \(= << V('rig.pbo.lowloss') >>\) (median \(\lambda =
<< V('rig.pbo.logit_med') >>\)).

\para{C7. Stationary block bootstrap} \citep{politis1994}: resample the daily series in blocks of geometric length
(mean 5 days), 10,000 draws; percentile CI. v2 OOS Sharpe: << V('v2.oos.sr_ci') >>, standard error
<< V('calc.boot.se') >>, \(P(\text{SR}\le 0) = << V('rig.boot.p') >>\).

\para{C8. Factor regression} \(r_t = \alpha + \beta_M\,\text{MktRF}_t + \beta_S\,\text{SMB}_t + \beta_H\,\text{HML}_t +
\beta_U\,\text{Mom}_t + \varepsilon_t\) on daily return on capital, Newey--West (5 lags) \citep{fama1993,carhart1997,newey1987}.
v2 IS (<< V('fac.n') >> days): \(\alpha = << V('calc.ff.alpha') >>\) a day (\(t = << V('fac.alpha_t') >>\)); \(\beta_M =
<< V('calc.ff.MktRF') >>\) (\(t = << V('calc.ff.MktRF.t') >>\)), \(\beta_S = << V('calc.ff.SMB') >>\), \(\beta_H =
<< V('calc.ff.HML') >>\), \(\beta_U = << V('calc.ff.Mom') >>\); \(R^2 = << V('fac.r2') >>\).

\para{C9. Taker fee} \(f(q) = r\,q(1-q)\) per share at price \(q\); per dollar of notional \(f/q = r(1-q)\), i.e.
\(10{,}000\,r(1-q)\) bps. At \(r = << V('fee.rate') >>\): \(q = 0.5\) pays << V('calc.fee.q50.c') >>¢ a share
(<< V('calc.fee.q50.bps') >>\,bps); \(q = 0.8\) pays << V('calc.fee.q80.c') >>¢ (<< V('calc.fee.q80.bps') >>\,bps).

\para{C10. Markov point leverage} Eq.~\ref{eq:lev}, with the match won probability computed exactly by recursion
over points, games, tiebreaks and sets (\texttt{src/markov.py}). Two even players who win << V('calc.mk.ps') >> of
service points: at the first point \(\Pr(\text{win}) = << V('calc.mk.start.p') >>\), moving to
<< V('calc.mk.start.up') >> or << V('calc.mk.start.dn') >>, so \(\Delta = << V('calc.mk.start.lev') >>\); serving at
5--5, 30--40 in the deciding set, \(\Pr(\text{win}) = << V('calc.mk.bp.p') >>\), moving to << V('calc.mk.bp.up') >>
or << V('calc.mk.bp.dn') >>: \(\Delta = << V('calc.mk.bp.lev') >>\). Mean \(|\Delta|\) over a match:
<< V('markov.lev') >>.

\para{C11. Latency budget} Eq.~\ref{eq:budget}. With the pre-registered \(L = << V('cv.pre.lag') >>\)\,s, \(D =
<< V('venue.delay') >>\)\,s and our measured \(\delta = << V('e2e.delta_s') >>\)\,s (pipeline plus network), a point
whose book reprices at the median \(R = << V('lat.book_vs_stamp_signed') >>\)\,s needs \(V < << V('calc.vmax.med') >>
+ \ell\): no feed wins it without an early call. At the 90th percentile \(R = << V('calc.R.p90') >>\)\,s, \(V <
<< V('calc.vmax.p90') >>\)\,s; the sweep's break-even (<< V('cv.pre.be.is') >>\,s IS) comes from such late reprices.

\para{C12. Capital and return on capital} Capital \(= 3\times\) the peak dollars locked in open positions (each
locked 4\,h, or until resolution). v2 IS: peak << V('calc.peak') >>, capital << V('v2.is.cap') >>; return \(= 365\,\bar
d/\text{capital} = 365 \times << V('calc.is.mean') >> / << V('v2.is.cap') >> = << V('calc.roc') >>\) a year.

\para{C13. Capacity and volume share} Capacity is the capital at which the seed-mean Sharpe falls to half its
smallest-size value along the size path; share \(=\) our notional per day \(/\) market volume per day. CV, post hoc,
IS, just below the half-Sharpe size: << V('capcv.notional') >> a day against << V('cap.inplay') >> of in-play volume
(<< V('capcv.share_inplay') >>) and << V('cap.fastq') >> traded by the fast tier 0--3\,s after a point
(<< V('capcv.share_fast') >>).

